:PD.Job menu.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STATUS'.Status of job
:P.The status of job shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CURUSER'.Current user profile
:P.The current user profile shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/IDENTITY'.Job user identity
:P.The job user identity shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SETBY'.Set by
:P.The set by shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ENTDATE'.Date
:P.The date shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ENTTIME'.Time
:P.The time shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STRDATE'.Date
:P.The date shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STRTIME'.Time
:P.The time shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBS'.Subsystem
:P.The subsystem shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBSPOOL'.Subsystem pool ID
:P.The subsystem pool ID shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TYPE'.Type of job
:P.The type of job shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SPCENV'.Special environment
:P.The special environment shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RTNCODE'.Program return code
:P.The program return code shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CNTRLD'.Controlled end requested
:P.The controlled end requested shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SYSPOOL'.System pool identifier
:P.The system pool identifier shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CPUMS'.Processing unit time used, in ms
:P.The processing unit time used, in ms shown for what the display is
about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/AUXIO'.Auxiliary I/O requests of the job
:P.The auxiliary I/O requests of the job shown for what the display is
about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBD'.Job description
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBDLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBQ'.Job queue
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBQLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBPTY'.Job priority (on job queue)
:P.The job priority (on job queue) shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OUTPTY'.Output priority (on output queue)
:P.The output priority (on output queue) shown for what the display is
about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ENDSEV'.End severity
:P.The end severity shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGLVL'.Level
:P.The level shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGSEV'.Severity
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGTXT'.Text
:P.The text shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGCLPGM'.Log CL program commands
:P.The log CL program commands shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGOUT'.Job log output
:P.The job log output shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PRTDEV'.Printer device
:P.The printer device shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OUTQ'.Default output queue
:P.The default output queue shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OUTQLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PRTTXT'.Printer text
:P.The printer text shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DATFMT'.Date format
:P.The format of dates&colon. the order of year, month and day.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DATSEP'.Date separator
:P.The character between the parts of a date.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TIMSEP'.Time separator
:P.The character between the parts of a time.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DECFMT'.Decimal format
:P.The decimal format&colon. the character used for the decimal point
and how zeros print before it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SWS'.Job switches
:P.The eight job switches&colon. 0 for off, 1 for on, X for unchanged.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/INQMSG'.Inquiry message reply
:P.How inquiry messages sent to the job are answered&colon. by the
operator, with their default replies, or from the system reply list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/BRKMSG'.Break message handling
:P.The break message handling shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STSMSG'.Status message
:P.The status message shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DEVRCY'.Device recovery action
:P.What happens to the job when its display device has an error&colon. a
message is sent, the request is ended, or the job is ended.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CCSID'.Coded character set identifier
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DFTCCSID'.Default coded character set identifier
:P.The default coded character set identifier shown for what the display
is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LANGID'.Language identifier
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CNTRYID'.Country or region identifier
:P.The country or region identifier shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SRTSEQ'.Sort sequence
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSGQMX'.Job message queue maximum size
:P.The job message queue maximum size shown for what the display is
about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSGQFL'.Job message queue full action
:P.What happens when the job's message queue fills&colon. the job ends,
the queue wraps, or messages are printed and then overwritten.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALWMLT'.Allow multiple threads
:P.The allow multiple threads shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SPLFACN'.Spooled file action
:P.What happens to the job's spooled files when the job ends&colon. they
are kept with the job or detached from it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RUNPTY'.Run priority
:P.The run priority of the job, from 1 (highest) to 99 (lowest).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TIMESLICE'.Time slice in milliseconds
:P.The time slice in milliseconds shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PURGE'.Eligible for purge
:P.Whether the job may be moved out of main storage when it waits for a
long time.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DFTWAIT'.Default wait time in seconds
:P.The default wait time in seconds shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CPUTIME'.Maximum CPU time in milliseconds
:P.The maximum CPU time in milliseconds shown for what the display is
about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CPUUSED'.CPU time used
:P.The CPU time used shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MAXTMP'.Maximum temporary storage in megabytes
:P.The maximum temporary storage in megabytes shown for what the display
is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TMPUSED'.Temporary storage used
:P.The temporary storage used shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TMPPEAK'.Peak temporary storage used
:P.The peak temporary storage used shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MAXTHD'.Maximum threads
:P.The maximum threads shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/THREADS'.Threads
:P.The threads shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/AFFGRP'.Group
:P.The group shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/AFFLVL'.Level
:P.The level shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RSCAFF'.Resources affinity group
:P.Whether the job's threads are kept together on the same processor
group.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SPLFKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F10=View 3
:PD.View 3.
:PT.F11=View 2
:PD.View 2.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F22=Printers
:PD.Runs WRKWTR.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F16=Job menu
:PD.Job menu.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SPLF/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FILE'.File
:P.The file, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DEVQ'.Device or Queue
:P.The device or Queue of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USRDTA'.User Data
:P.User data, up to 10 characters, kept with the object.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SPLSTS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PAGES'.Total Pages
:P.The total Pages of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CURPAGE'.Current Page
:P.The current Page of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/COPIES'.Copies
:P.How many copies are printed.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SPLF/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Send
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to send it. The Send Network
Spooled File (SNDNETSPLF) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Spooled File Attr (CHGSPLFA) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Spooled
File (HLDSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Spooled File (DLTSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Spooled File (DSPSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Spooled File (RLSSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.7=Messages
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to messages it.
:PT.8=Attributes
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to attributes it. The Work
with Spooled File Attributes (WRKSPLFA) command runs for the entry.
:PT.9=Work with printing status
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to work with printing status
it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/LOGKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
